  "content": [
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 2,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "market a pool -- Or, gate, Nehemiah 3:1; 12:39"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 3,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "waiting for -- The Sinai MS. omits \"waiting for the moving of the water.\" and all of John 5:4."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 4,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "For -- See margin ref. (See Scofield \"John 5:3\")\n\nangel -- See note, (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\")"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 14,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "sin -- Sin. (See Scofield \"Romans 3:23\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 18,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "his Father -- (Greek - βιβλαρίδιον,\" his own Father). The Jews understood perfectly that Jesus was claiming to be God. Cf. John 10:33."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 31,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "witness -- Cf. John 8:14. In John 5:31 our Lord, defending His Messianic claims before Jews who denied those claims, accepts the biblical rule of evidence, which required \"two witnesses\"; John 8:17; Numbers 35:30; Deuteronomy 17:6. A paraphrase of verse John 5:31 would be: \"If I bear witness of myself ye will say my witness is not true.\" Cf. John 8:14."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 34,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "saved -- (See Scofield \"Romans 1:16\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 37,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "seen -- Cf.\n\n(See Scofield \"John 1:18\")."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
